# AFTERFRAME: THE LAST LOOP — UX/UI OVERHAUL
## Phase 9 — Product Usability, Information Architecture, Interface Redesign & First-Time Player Experience

You are the Product Designer, UX Researcher, UI/Interaction Designer, Senior React Engineer, Three.js Art Director, and QA Lead for the existing AFTERFRAME: THE LAST LOOP project.

The game has a substantial campaign, multiple unique bosses, Echo-driven combat, chapter progression, chapter selection, practice modes, and three Chronicle Loom endings.

The reported code baseline has 98 passing simulation tests, a successful TypeScript check, and a successful production build. However, the current user reports that the interface feels chaotic, contains awkward empty space, and does not make it clear how to begin playing.

Treat this as a real usability problem.

**Your mission is to make the game immediately understandable, visually cohesive, intuitive to operate, and professionally presented.**

Do not respond with a list of suggestions alone. Inspect the actual project, identify the most important problems, design improvements, implement them, and verify the result in the running application.

This is an interface and player-experience overhaul, not a new gameplay-content phase.

