# 16. Definition of done

The UX/UI overhaul is complete only when:

- A new player can identify how to start from the title screen without outside help.
- Campaign, Continue, Chapter Select, Practice, Controls, and Settings have a clear hierarchy.
- The intro leads to a visibly playable state with a clear next objective.
- HUD information is prioritized and contextual.
- Tutorial hints match the current objective and actual controls.
- The major empty-space and layout issues observed in the audit have been corrected deliberately.
- Pause, victory, defeat, retry, and ending interactions are coherent.
- Desktop and mobile screens look intentionally composed.
- Gameplay inputs, progression, resource behavior, and encounter mechanics remain intact.
- All 98 existing regression tests remain present and passing.
- TypeScript and production build pass.
- Actual browser usability scenarios are completed and reported honestly.
- Before/after visual evidence is supplied where available.
- The audit, implementation, and test results are saved in the actual workspace.

